  "coarsening": "For every full k7 candidate, enumerate all 35 single-triple unions to k5. Choose unions on pilot development evidence only. Do not tune unions on confirmation. This repeats the winning single-triple merge family; a merged partition differs from flat k5.",
  "controlled_full": "Same raw k7,q=1/3,alpha=.625 and original confirmation sample/fit seeds. Align raw seven-centre point labels to that wave centred point, then apply its frozen five-cluster map. Refits align to their own raw point before the frozen map.",
  "controlled_worry": "Same q=.75 hierarchy and original prepared pilot/confirmation masses/seeds. Align the three raw parents to the original three-parent assignment on the common reference, and split parent C2 with raw five-question two-centre kmeans. This is a fixed-parent diagnostic, not a new natural thematic claim.",
  "date": "2026-11-20",
  "evaluation": "Ordinary count ARI, weighted matched Jaccard per cluster; within-wave all distinct run pairs, cross-wave all products. Report all runs and failures. Structural shares are native point shares.",
  "families": {
    "full": [
      2021,
      2023,
      2025
    ],
    "worry": [
      2019,
      2021,
      2023,
      2025
    ]
  },
  "fit": "Independent per-wave weighted Lloyd kmeans; 20 initializations; max_iter 300; full tol 1e-4, worry tol zero; no imputation or variance standardization.",
  "heldout": "No held-out respondents or outcomes used anywhere in this development sensitivity study.",
  "identity": "||x-y||^2 = ||(x-mean(x))-(y-mean(y))||^2 + d*(mean(x)-mean(y))^2. Full centred mean coefficient 1 -> raw 6; worry parent 1.5 -> raw 5; worry child 0 -> raw 5.",
  "point_screen": {
    "dominance_exclusive_maximum": 3,
    "maximum_share": 0.45,
    "min_point_ARI": 0.62,
    "min_point_Jaccard": 0.5
  },
  "protection": "No edits to manuscript, publication website, current companions, frozen models or earlier results; no Git commits or uploads.",
  "question": "What changes when respondent-wise worry centring and mean downweighting are removed?",
  "raw": "Numeric worry scores divided by sqrt(d), with alpha in the full family, and NO appended mean coordinate.",
  "reselection_hierarchy": "Fit raw k3 parents; split the parent ranked 0,1,2 by mean centre level in the 2025 point fit. Transfer the parent index by maximum-overlap correspondence; each wave fits its own parent and child centres. Child uses the same q and raw geometry. Refits match parent labels to their own wave point before selecting the child population.",
  "rules": "Exhaustive ordered DNF cost<=3; precision>=.80 in every native wave; within .01 of best 2025 coverage minimize cost, -precision2025, -coverage2025, question count, canonical JSON. Extract for controlled and selected raw models without changing cluster assignments.",
  "samples": "Paired with saved original schedules and weights. Pilot 8 and independent confirmation 50 draws of each type. Same eligible development respondents and country weights. Same 2025 reference for every pair.",
